### IPP-1707 Backup keeps the date of "done" questions
### Put ADMIN_PASSWORD from server/.env while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back.
### Use the LOCAL database only (step 4 restores into it).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = changeme
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Admin login -> 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 2. Browser: Admin -> Backup -> Download full backup.
###    Open the file -> users[].done[] items now have "at": "<date>" (when the question was marked done).
###    Older backup files without "at" still restore (date = restore time, same as before).

### 3. MongoDB Compass (local "interview-prep" DB): delete a TEST user who has done questions (users collection),
###    then Admin -> Backup -> restore the file from step 2 -> "users added: 1".

### 4. Admin -> Users -> that user -> Details -> Study progress:
###    "Last studied", "This week" and "Recently done" dates are the OLD dates, not today.
